\title{Truth table for negation}
\date{2025-12-16T02:02:14Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Remark}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{We can summarize the [definition of negation](002W) with a \em{truth table} showing
the truth value of #{\neg P} for each possible value of #{P}:
##{\begin{array}{cc}P & \neg P \\ \hline \True & \False \\ \False & \True \end{array}}
}

\p{In general, a \em{truth table} is a table showing the value of some expression for every possible combination of values for some variables.  In this case, there is only one variable, so the table only has two rows—one for #{P = \True} and one for #{P = \False}.}

